questions.question_text:
How many axes (lines) of symmetry does this shape have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,1.7)--(1.05,0.15)--(0,-1.35)--(-1.05,0.15)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

How many axes (lines) of symmetry does this shape have?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-0.6,-1.6)--(0.6,-1.6)--(0.6,-0.6)--(1.6,-0.6)--(1.6,0.6)--(0.6,0.6)--(0.6,1.6)--(-0.6,1.6)--(-0.6,0.6)--(-1.6,0.6)--(-1.6,-0.6)--(-0.6,-0.6)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What is the order of rotational symmetry of this shape?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (90:1.6)--(141.43:1.6)--(192.86:1.6)--(244.29:1.6)--(295.71:1.6)--(347.14:1.6)--(38.57:1.6)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

What is the order of rotational symmetry of this shape?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (-1.5,-1.0)--(1.5,-1.0)--(0.8,1.0)--(-0.8,1.0)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue,domain=-1.5:1.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{-0.9*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue] (-1.0,2.0)--(1.0,-2.0);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue] (-1.9,1.1)--(1.9,1.1);
\draw[<->,thick,blue] (-1.9,-1.1)--(1.9,-1.1);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Does this graph have line symmetry about the $y$-axis, rotational symmetry about the origin, both, or neither?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue,domain=-0.5:2.1,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.9*(\x-0.8)*(\x-0.8)});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Which line is the axis of symmetry of the parabola below?
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw[<->] (-2.2,0)--(2.2,0);
\draw[<->] (0,-2.2)--(0,2.2);
\draw[<->,thick,blue,domain=-1.5:1.5,smooth,variable=\x,samples=60] plot ({\x},{0.9*\x*\x});
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

State the number of lines of symmetry and the order of rotational symmetry of this shape.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\draw (0,0)--(1.7,0.25)--(1.2,1.15)--cycle;
\draw (0,0)--(-1.7,-0.25)--(-1.2,-1.15)--cycle;
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
